# Frontend build-time settings (Vite). Copy to .env.local for local use; on Vercel set it in
# Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables. Contains no secrets: it is a public URL.
#
# Leave UNSET when the UI is served by the backend itself (Render single-service) or run via `npm run dev`
# (the Vite dev server proxies /api to http://127.0.0.1:8000).
#
# Set it when the UI is hosted on a different origin than the API, e.g. UI on Vercel + API on Render.
# No trailing slash needed (it is stripped). The backend must then allow the UI's origin via CORS_ORIGINS.
# NOTE: Vite inlines this at build time -- changing it on Vercel requires a fresh redeploy.
VITE_API_BASE=https://your-backend.onrender.com
